    {'title': 'Modern CSS Layout Assessment', 'category': 'Modern CSS Layout', 'domain': 'Web Development', 'difficulty': 'Intermediate', 'description': 'Flexbox, CSS Grid, container queries, subgrid, and alignment properties.', 'time_limit_minutes': 15, 'passing_score': 70, 'icon': 'fas fa-table-cells-large', 'badge_icon': 'fas fa-award', 'questions': [{'text': 'In CSS Flexbox, what property aligns flex items along the main axis?', 'options': ['align-items', 'justify-content', 'align-content', 'flex-wrap'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'justify-content distributes space and aligns items along the primary flex axis.'}, {'text': 'In CSS Grid, how do you create a responsive column layout that automatically fits as many 250px columns as possible without media queries?', 'options': ['grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));', 'grid-columns: auto 250px;', 'grid-template-rows: repeat(12, 1fr);', 'flex-wrap: wrap;'], 'correct': 0, 'explanation': 'repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)) dynamically tiles columns based on container width.'}, {'text': 'What is the difference between CSS Media Queries and CSS Container Queries (@container)?', 'options': ['Container queries test device battery level.', 'Media queries query the overall viewport/browser size, whereas Container queries query the size of a specific parent container element.', 'Media queries only work on mobile.', 'There is no difference.'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'Container queries allow styling components based on the size of their parent container.'}, {'text': 'What does `gap: 16px;` do in Flexbox and Grid layouts?', 'options': ['Adds margin to the outer parent container.', 'Creates consistent spacing between grid tracks or flex items without child margin hacks.', 'Sets line height.', 'Adds internal padding to all children.'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'The gap property defines row and column spacing between layout items.'}, {'text': 'What does CSS Grid `subgrid` enable?', 'options': ['Rendering an embedded HTML iframe.', 'Allowing nested child grids to inherit and align directly with the track definition of the parent grid.', 'Exporting grid layout to PDF.', 'Creating 3D WebGL canvases.'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'subgrid allows child items to share the column and row tracks of their parent grid.'}]},
