    {'title': 'Vue.js Web Assessment', 'category': 'Vue.js', 'domain': 'Web Development', 'difficulty': 'Intermediate', 'description': 'Vue 3 Composition API, reactivity system (ref/reactive), Pinia state, and Single File Components.', 'time_limit_minutes': 15, 'passing_score': 70, 'icon': 'fab fa-vuejs', 'badge_icon': 'fas fa-award', 'questions': [{'text': 'In Vue 3 Composition API, what is the difference between `ref()` and `reactive()`?', 'options': ['`ref()` wraps primitives or objects in a reactive reference accessible via `.value`; `reactive()` creates a reactive Proxy object for collections/objects directly.', '`ref()` is read-only.', '`reactive()` is deprecated.', 'There is no difference.'], 'correct': 0, 'explanation': 'ref() handles both primitive and object values via a .value getter/setter; reactive() proxies complex objects.'}, {'text': 'What lifecycle hook in Vue 3 Composition API replaces `mounted()` from the Options API?', 'options': ['onMounted()', 'created()', 'setupMounted()', 'init()'], 'correct': 0, 'explanation': 'The onMounted() hook registers a callback to be executed once the component DOM is inserted.'}, {'text': 'What is the official state management library recommended for Vue 3 applications?', 'options': ['Vuex 3', 'Pinia', 'Redux', 'MobX'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'Pinia is the official, intuitive, lightweight, and type-safe state management library for Vue 3.'}, {'text': 'What directive is used for two-way data binding on form inputs in Vue?', 'options': ['v-bind', 'v-model', 'v-on', 'v-slot'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'v-model simplifies two-way synchronization between form controls and component reactive state.'}, {'text': 'What does the `computed()` function in Vue 3 do?', 'options': ['Calculates random numbers.', 'Creates a cached reactive property that only re-evaluates when its reactive dependencies change.', 'Executes async API calls.', 'Styles CSS animations.'], 'correct': 1, 'explanation': 'Computed properties are lazily evaluated and cached based on their reactive dependencies.'}]},
